  "decisions": {
    "k-php2shell": {
      "decision": "created",
      "narrativeId": "n-php2shell",
      "reason": "Created n-php2shell, replacing Flying Tesla Roadster (paused) at the six-narrative cap. Four pump.fun coins whose own metadata names the story: PHP-UP-2026 (description about the exploit), two coins named PHP2SHELL and Saviour of the Internet (SURY; description names PHP2Shell). Rolling 24h volume at discovery about $12.4M ($6.7M, $1.4M, $1.3M, $3.0M), market caps $71K to $1.3M, no quarantine flag; the cluster the script found (SURY and the two PHP2SHELL coins, $5.6M) plus PHP-UP-2026, which was this lead's deferred coin from the previous report. Independent sources beyond the metadata: Rapid7's post that the PHP project announced security releases for CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619 (2026-10-21 15:35 UTC), a Register article relayed by a security-news account, and several researchers' posts (e1:8, e2:0). The previous report's deferral (cap full, pools under an hour old) no longer applies: the release happened and the pools are 6 to 26 hours old."
    },
    "k-fees": {
      "decision": "rejected",
      "reason": "SURY (fees to a GitHub maintainer), ORBIO (half of fees converted to inference credits), CLOUT (60% of fees to creators) and OGDOGE share only the word fees; four different fee designs, no common story. SURY joins the PHP2Shell narrative on its PHP2Shell description, not on this word."
    },
    "k-credits": {
      "decision": "rejected",
      "reason": "SURY, ORBIO and RAETO share only the word credits (emergency patch credit, inference credits, inference credits for stock holders); no common story. The Borly/ORBIO AI-compute lead was dropped from the daily searches after two empty runs."
    },
    "k-using": {
      "decision": "rejected",
      "reason": "Au (a fusion-to-gold meme; the search e2:1 returned only call-group promotion and gold-forex posts), SHADOW (private payments on Solana) and GTA (\"Deployed using j7tracker\") share only the word using; no common story and no independent source."
    },
    "k-launches": {
      "decision": "rejected",
      "reason": "NOOX (a trading agent that scouts new pump.fun launches), CLOUT (an AI influencer platform) and KYRO (a dashboard that tracks new token launches) are three unrelated tools; the e2:2 search returned call-group promotion and an unrelated Nox operating-system project."
    },
    "k-create": {
      "decision": "rejected",
      "reason": "CLOUT, CREORA (private AI chat and image tools) and OGDOGE share only the word create; the e2:3 search returned call-group promotion and an unrelated Claude-skills post."
    },
    "k-private": {
      "decision": "rejected",
      "reason": "CREORA (private AI; posts say 10,000 sign-ups and a Dash payment AMA, e2:4), SHADOW (private payments) and DRKW (a private wallet) are three different products that share the word private; combined volume $972K but no common story."
